Hello everyone We are glad to inform you that we have finally released the long-awaited update. There was silence for half a year for a reason, we actively worked and reworked the game. Now Beetle Nest is a 3rd person shooter, the whole game has been rethought by us and taken to a new level. The entire general technical base is ready, now we will fix bugs, add new content and expand the game.

Now about what has been done:
- All models and textures have been changed;
- Completely redesigned lighting;
- Changed the basic mechanics of the character, now everything is from the 3rd person;
- Added transport;
- All buildings have been changed and new ones have been added;
- New AI for all enemies;
- Added a new pirate faction;
- All enemies are now always on the map, they do not disappear anywhere, they are at enmity with each other and interfere with you;
- Geometry rendering is now entirely on the graphics card;
- Added RTX support;
- New technology of virtual shadows and textures;
- Multithreaded rendering;
- No LOD and rendering range, all characters and objects can always be seen, even if you are very far away;
- Time of day system;
- Volumetric clouds;
- A new economic system with an exchange and resource extraction;
- The exchange works in real time and is always updated, your actions directly affect the exchange rate;
- All resources now have physical objects, they need to be collected and delivered;
- New inertial animations for the character;
- ...
And much more. We will gradually post posts about the new update, as there is a lot of content.

Major changes:
- Biomass has been removed;
- Added a resource exchange;
- The method of obtaining crystals has been changed;
- The exchange post has been removed;
- Added the "Local Farm" building;
- The construction of the "Mine" has been changed and redesigned.

The economic system has undergone significant changes. Now enemies do not provide resources, and materials for improvements and exchange can be found in the world. The materials themselves can only be moved by means of transport, which has loading and unloading drones. After collecting resources, they must be delivered to the nearest outpost, which has a reactor. There is a special unloading area at the outpost, from where your resources will be picked up by a delivery ship and transported to the main station.

Now you can get money in several ways. The easiest way is to complete some kind of cleanup or search task. But the most profitable will be the collection and processing of resources from local farms, which are different on each planet.

Crystals for improvements are now mined only in mines and do not appear in clusters. The mines yield crates of crystals at the exit, which will also need to be transported to the outpost to conserve resources.

In the future, the economic system will be improved and supplemented. Further development will be aimed at fighting for resources with local inhabitants.

Yesterday I finished developing the landscape for the first planet. I thought for a long time why the characters don't really fit into the environment, but then I remembered that this is still space. As a result, I changed the entire color scheme of the environment and changed the approach to vegetation. Maroon, lilac and turquoise colors now prevail. Each planet will have its own recognizable style.

I decided to increase the map in size and now it is 16 square kilometers. There used to be 4 squares. There are 11 outposts scattered on the planet, which are randomly generated. In addition to outposts, side buildings were made to help in development and encourage exploration of the planet. There are also plans to add some collectible plant seeds that can be collected on different planets and grown on the ship to produce products from them and sell on the stock exchange.

The exchange will be another innovation and will replace the existing economic system with a more interesting one.

Outposts will have 5 types of generation:
- A new outpost;
- An empty outpost;
- Destroyed outpost;
- An outpost captured by pirates;
- A bug-infested outpost.

In the case of the new outpost, no action will be required to turn on the protection and reactor. An empty outpost can be reactivated using a generator. The generator will be a small mini-game. If the launch is successful, the turrets on the towers will turn on and all the doors in the buildings will open. But if the launch was unsuccessful, then everything within a radius of 20 kilometers will be destroyed :) A nuclear reactor is not to be trifled with.
The destroyed outpost will have a chance to spawn open and whole buildings, inside which you can find weapons or useful resources. Captured outposts can also be reactivated, but this will require them to be cleared of enemies. In the case of pirates, you can take their resources for yourself and send them to the base.

Also, do not worry about moving around the map. I have previously written about transport, which is already fully implemented and will be available to the player from the very beginning.

Hello everyone, so I've completed a new update that has brought a lot of new changes to the game. 
Short and concise:

- Complete change of interface styling;
- Spacecraft recycling;
- New farm ship module;
- New third-person view mode;
- Redesigned the mechanics of improvements;
- Some models have been redesigned;
- Balancing of some devices has been carried out;
- Improved performance.

Now let's talk in more detail about each innovation.

Finally, a style has been found that will suit the game, and it will stay with us for a long time throughout the game. Now it is more futuristic, has sharp corners and edges, as well as all the graphics along with the models. Along with the new interface came the convenience of using many elements that had previously been made not quite successfully.

The spacecraft has been almost completely redesigned and optimized as much as possible. Now it looks exactly as intended, but in the future I will improve it a little more, as new updates will be released that will require more monitors and space for themselves on the ship itself.

One of the most important innovations is the farm. Crystals or plants can be grown on the farm.    There are now 3 types of crystals: energy, earth and quantum. All of them will be needed to upgrade the clones and the farm. There are only one plants now, but they will be added in the future with regular updates. The existing plant is necessary for processing into bio-fuel. Bio-fuel can be sold for good money, but for this you will have to make the delivery yourself. Here we come to the next innovation.

A third-person view will be available during the delivery of bio-fuel to one of the planets. You will need to make your way to the factory through space pirates. At the same time, you will need to keep an eye on the mobile container, which may lag behind you. Three types of devices and clones will help you with this, which will come to the rescue if you can get close to the factory. Shipping is a difficult task, but extremely profitable. This mission starts with only one life, and if you die during it, the barrels will disappear, and you will be returned to the ship.

As mentioned above, we now have 3 types of crystals, and now each improvement will require a different type of crystal. You can grow them both on the farm and get them during the main missions. In honor of this change, the crystal models and icons were redesigned.

There was also a small balancing of some devices, but it is almost insignificant and designed for what I'm going to do with them in the future.

And the last thing. I've been able to improve performance a little bit, but things will get even better in the future.
